4. Close SDK gaps for local MCP plugin lifecycle
   Scope: ensure the public SDK owns local project initialization, SQLite migrations, encrypted credential/token storage, MCP source install, OAuth connect/reconnect/refresh, no-auth MCP support, discovery, indexing, lexical/BM25 search, schema lookup, invocation, and structured status/errors. Explore implementation details as needed, but keep app-specific behavior out of SDK internals.
